  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the dominant uncertainty is whether the image modality is informative at all and whether it could complement or outperform RNA. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides the cleanest direct comparison: same profile setting (single), a standard pretrained encoder (ResNet-50), isolating the modality effect. If image accuracy is comparable or better than RNA, multimodal fusion becomes a promising direction to exploit in later experiments. If image is substantially worse, we can focus remaining budget on improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt) and aggregation. This single experiment reduces the most critical uncertainty with minimal confounding, making it the highest-information choice for experiment 2 of 10."
}

